I'm a tinkerer who loves all things computer and math. I mainly mess around with TypeScript, JavaScript, [Zig](https://ziglang.org/) and C in my free time. 

My area of interests are **computer architecture**, **JavaScript tooling**, **compilers** and **systems programming**.

I'm currently writing my own [JavaScript framework in Zig](https://github.com/elyfheim/lassi) (still a work-in-progress). Planning to have seamless integration with Zig codes so the users can easily 
write performant logic in WebAssemby, should they choose to do so.

Professionally, I mostly work with web technologies ranging from various front-end tooling like [React](https://react.dev/) and [Vue](https://react.dev/) to back-end services and infrastructures-related technologies.

I'm quite obsessed with workflow optimization and ergonomics, I got into split keyboards in [2025](https://elyfheim.me/blog/split-keyboard/) and I think it's game-changing for my typing experience. 
And naturally I also prefer a keyboard-focused editor like [neovim](https://neovim.io/) (although, [helix](https://helix-editor.com/) is looking really nice these days).

### Projects
- [Warlock](https://warlock.elyfheim.me): A CHIP-8 emulator/interpreter written in C, compiled to WebAssembly.
- [Lassi](https://github.com/elyfheim/lassi): A JavaScript framework with Vue-inspired syntax, fine-grained reactivity and no virtual DOM overhead. Written in Zig. 
- [Nordle](https://nordle.elyfheim.me): A Wordle clone built with React, written in TypeScript.
- [Nordle (Lassi)](https://github.com/elyfheim/nordle-lassi): Nordle, but built with my own JavaScript framework, Lassi.

